<title>USA: N.J. courts say need $10 mln more -- paper.</title>
<headline>N.J. courts say need $10 mln more -- paper.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-04-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>New Jersey court officials said they need $10 million more than the Whitman Administration's proposal for next year's budget, the Star Ledger reported Thursday.</p>
<p>The figures came out in the first round of departmental budget hearings in Trenton, before the Senate Budget and Appropriations Committee.</p>
<p>The court system's budget for the current fiscal year included a $10 million carryover from the previous budget. But the one-shot was not replaced in the fiscal 1998 $347.5 million budget proposal, resulting in threats of layoffs.</p>
<p>--Steven Dickson, 212-859-1652</p>
